Z||000003||Dingo||03-27-2001||10:06 AM||||For what ever reason I thought folks were using only the electronics. Just took a look at my first Fiero with a Northstar in it. Nice!  What years work best? What size is the motor and what is the weight compared to the stock V6. Is this like any other V8 conversion or are there other things you need to make, cut, etc. ? This might be the route I will go.<P>thanks||||reg||10
Z||000004||FieroLisa||03-27-2001||01:07 PM||||All I can say is 300 hp.<BR> It's DAMN fun to drive.||||reg||1
Z||000005||northstar87||03-27-2001||01:59 PM||||The engine swap looks really clean.  I love this conversion so much I just finished my 2nd one.  It is such a nice compromise.  I only gained 200lbs, 24 miles per gallon, still have my trunk, 13 second car, air conditioning and cruise control,(I could not use it much because I always had to keep up with Lisa!  She can drive!),can drive it across the country with no problems, (I think I did this Week, RIGHT LISA??), Nothing will break because it is all Caddy.  Just a nice conversion.  It is kind of expensive though.  Just do your homework before making a choice.<P>Chris Moore<BR>ASE Master Auto Tech and Auto Instructor||||reg||1
